The key to piloting Jenova, Ancient Calamity is understanding its core engine: Jenova targets a creature each combat to place +1/+1 counters equal to Jenova's power and make it a Mutant. When that Mutant dies on your turn, you draw cards equal to its power, creating a self-fueling card draw and sacrifice engine.
This is a Bracket 3 build running three Game Changers: Demonic Tutor, Vampiric Tutor, Ancient Tomb. It contains zero mass land denial and focuses on high-synergy board development, interactive answers, and an inevitable endgame clock.

# Commander and Core Synergy
Jenova, Ancient Calamity :: primary commander driving the deck's core strategy
Hardened Scales :: critical engine card maximizing commander synergy and card advantage
Branching Evolution :: critical engine card maximizing commander synergy and card advantage
Corpsejack Menace :: critical engine card maximizing commander synergy and card advantage
Skullclamp :: critical engine card maximizing commander synergy and card advantage
Greater Good :: critical engine card maximizing commander synergy and card advantage

# High-Impact Engines and Support
Ashnod's Altar :: premier support piece providing board presence, ramp, or recursion
Heroic Intervention :: premier support piece providing board presence, ramp, or recursion
Assassin's Trophy :: premier support piece providing board presence, ramp, or recursion
Beast Within :: premier support piece providing board presence, ramp, or recursion

# Game Changers and Interaction
Demonic Tutor :: high-power Game Changer providing irreplaceable tempo, draw, or board control
Vampiric Tutor :: high-power Game Changer providing irreplaceable tempo, draw, or board control
Ancient Tomb :: high-power Game Changer providing irreplaceable tempo, draw, or board control
Arcane Signet :: efficient interaction and acceleration keeping the table in check
Sol Ring :: efficient interaction and acceleration keeping the table in check
